WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:06.160
Will the Byrdes survive "Ozark"? Will the cartel&nbsp;
or the FBI catch up with Marty first? Or will Ruth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:11.600
kill just about everyone? What you need to know&nbsp;
about "Ozark" Season 4 Part 2, straight ahead.

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.640
Season 4 is the first season of&nbsp;
"Ozark" to be split into two parts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.640 --> 00:00:20.640
but fans fearing an extended half-time&nbsp;
hiatus needn't worry too much.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.960
Instead of making us wait for the back half of&nbsp;
the final "Ozark" season, Netflix is gearing up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.080
to drop the second set of episodes on April&nbsp;
29, a mere three months after Part 1 aired.

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:35.280
"Ozark" premiered its first season in July 2017,&nbsp;
and returned for its sophomore season in August&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:40.240
of the next year. The third season arrived on&nbsp;
March 27, 2020. Considering "Ozark" wrapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.800
production on Season 4 back in October 2020,&nbsp;
it was always a possibility that we'd see an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.520
accelerated release schedule, but nobody thought&nbsp;
we'd be watching the end of Marty Byrde's journey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.640
as early as April 2022. Netflix definitely&nbsp;
deserves a big pat on the back for this one.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:59.360
The second half of "Ozark" Season 4 is&nbsp;
expected to feature all of the regular&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:03.040
cast members from the first half, with&nbsp;
the obvious exception of those who did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:06.560
not make it out of the first seven&nbsp;
episodes alive. All four members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.720
the Byrde family are expected to return,&nbsp;
including Marty, played by Jason Bateman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.040
Wendy, played by Laura Linney, and the&nbsp;
couple's children, Charlotte and Jonah.

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:20.160
Season 4's seventh episode, "Sanctified,"&nbsp;
saw the untimely deaths of Wyatt Langmore and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:24.480
Darlene Snell-Langmore. This sadly leaves&nbsp;
Ruth Langmore as one of the last members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:28.960
of her clan left standing. Julia Garner&nbsp;
has won praise for her portrayal of Ruth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:33.920
earning two consecutive Primetime Emmy Awards for&nbsp;
Outstanding Supporting Actress in a Drama Series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:36.400
We also think it's safe to say&nbsp;
that Wyatt's younger brother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.840
Three, will make an appearance at some&nbsp;
point in the final seven episodes.

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:44.320
It's unclear if Omar Navarro or Special&nbsp;
Agent Maya Miller will reappear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.760
especially as Navarro was arrested&nbsp;
by Miller in the mid-season finale.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:49.440
"Don't forget about me."

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:54.800
But even if they don't return, plenty of&nbsp;
emissaries of the FBI and the Navarro cartel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:59.520
remain. Additional characters we expect to see&nbsp;
back in the final seven episodes of the series&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:05.360
include Javi Elizonndro, private investigator&nbsp;
Mel Sattem, Jim Rattelsdorf, and Hannah Clay.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:10.240
We also wouldn't be shocked to see Richard Thomas&nbsp;
return once more as Wendy's father, Nathan Davis.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:15.520
The final seven episodes of "Ozark" have a&nbsp;
lot hanging on the line for the Byrde family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.520 --> 00:02:19.520
While the FBI's deal with Javi would seem&nbsp;
to be working for them at the moment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.160
a closer inspection would probably reveal&nbsp;
that the deal is only hanging on by a thread.

00:02:26.080 --> 00:02:27.920
"And I really wanna kill you, you know?"

00:02:28.880 --> 00:02:33.040
Ruth has never been more distant from Marty&nbsp;
than she is after Javi murders Wyatt in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.320
mid-season finale. After she finds Wyatt and&nbsp;
Darlene's bodies, Ruth holds Marty at gunpoint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.320 --> 00:02:42.480
and demands that he tells her who killed&nbsp;
them. Marty and Wendy refuse to tell her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:45.600
but Jonah quickly outs his&nbsp;
parents' boss as a murderer.

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:47.120
"His name is Javi Elizonndro."

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.080
In the final scene of the episode,&nbsp;
Ruth promises to kill Javi and screams,

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.880
"If you want to stop me, you're&nbsp;
gonna have to f—ing kill me!"

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.120
While Ruth, Marty, and Wendy&nbsp;
have tussled in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:05.600
this seems like a definitive breaking point for&nbsp;
the two. Wendy and Marty are also going to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:10.320
to deal with Jonah's continued rebelliousness.&nbsp;
The young money launderer has previously shown&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.080
that he is more loyal to Ruth than his own&nbsp;
parents, something that seems to bother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.200
Wendy even more than Marty. We also expect&nbsp;
plenty of political machinations by Wendy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.840
along with the family lawyer, Jim Rattelsdorf.&nbsp;
Since the beginning of Season 4, Wendy has led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:28.480
the Byrde Foundation as a means of growing&nbsp;
the family's wealth, power, and influence.

00:03:28.480 --> 00:03:31.520
At some point, "Ozark" will also&nbsp;
have to catch up to the Season 4&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.520 --> 00:03:35.440
opening scene which shows a disastrous&nbsp;
car crash involving all four members of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:39.040
the Byrde family. Do you really think&nbsp;
they're all going to make it out alive?

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:45.120
Mel Sattem, played by Adam Rothenberg, is&nbsp;
relentless, yet he somehow manages to stay calm,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:50.000
cool, and collected in the process. The former cop&nbsp;
turned private investigator will stop at nothing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:55.280
to track down Helen Pierce as he was hired by her&nbsp;
estranged husband to discover her whereabouts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:59.840
As a refresher, Helen was the Navarro cartel's&nbsp;
attorney when Omar decided to have her killed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.320
allowing the Byrde family to live. All the&nbsp;
same, Mel continuously talks to anyone who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:08.640
will hear him out as he presumably just&nbsp;
needs to know where Helen is, alive or dead.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:12.960
Perhaps most intriguing of all is the&nbsp;
fact that Mel has been talking to the FBI.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.920
Though it would be ideal to see&nbsp;
the Byrde family make it out alive,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:20.560
they have dug themselves some pretty big holes&nbsp;
throughout "Ozark," and it's seemingly only a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:25.440
matter of time before they get caught for one of&nbsp;
their many crimes. Still, fans will have to wait&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:30.000
and see if Mel gets his signature, or whether he&nbsp;
might play a role in sinking the Byrde family.

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.680
Ruth is, for better or worse, on a rampage.&nbsp;
She's lost virtually all of her family members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.680 --> 00:04:39.920
and Wyatt's death is her breaking point. After&nbsp;
all, she threatens the Byrdes with a gun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:39.920 --> 00:04:43.040
and viewers last see her on&nbsp;
the verge of seeking revenge.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:47.360
Though Javi is vicious, ill-tempered,&nbsp;
and seemingly thinks he's untouchable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:50.880
audience members have come to discover&nbsp;
that you don't mess with Ruth Langmore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.360
and a showdown between the two would be&nbsp;
pretty sweet, assuming Ruth comes out on top.

00:04:55.360 --> 00:05:00.000
If she did, however, actually pull off her&nbsp;
revenge, chaos and madness would likely ensue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.240
First and foremost, killing the head of the&nbsp;
cartel is typically frowned upon. Secondly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:09.440
the Byrde family has a deal with the FBI, which&nbsp;
could be jeopardized if Javi was to go down.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:14.160
At that point, would the FBI have any&nbsp;
reason not to take Marty and Wendy down too?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:18.160
Ruth may have been a trusted ally at one&nbsp;
point, but Marty and Wendy likely don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.080
want their deal to collapse, despite&nbsp;
Javi being arguably the most savage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:26.160
enemy of the Byrde family to date. Only&nbsp;
time will tell if Ruth gets her revenge.

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:31.600
This family's tensions aren't due to everyday&nbsp;
elements. Wendy and Jonah aren't at odds&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.640
because Wendy won't let Jonah, say, extend his&nbsp;
curfew. Life-altering mistakes have been made,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:39.520
trust has been destroyed, and people have died.

00:05:39.520 --> 00:05:41.200
"I think you have Stockholm Syndrome."

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.920
Jonah has rightfully been rebellious in Season&nbsp;
4, and he wants nothing to do with his mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:50.240
to boot, since he believes she had his uncle&nbsp;
killed. Wendy didn't make matters any better&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:50.240 --> 00:05:55.600
when she tried to have Jonah arrested, but Marty&nbsp;
luckily was able to put out that familial fire.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:59.280
Surely, Jonah giving up Javi's name to&nbsp;
Ruth won't sit well with the family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.280 --> 00:06:02.240
Although Charlotte seems to be&nbsp;
all-in on the family business,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.160
this has only further pushed Jonah&nbsp;
away. Wendy might be more concerned&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:11.040
with her political ambitions right now, but her&nbsp;
family has seemingly witnessed irreparable damage.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:15.440
One thing is for sure, and that's that no&nbsp;
one is safe. The car crash at the beginning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.440 --> 00:06:19.280
of Season 4 looked fatal. It's largely&nbsp;
speculation right now, but it would be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.280 --> 00:06:23.840
a shame if the Byrdes finally reunited, just&nbsp;
for one of them to be taken out by that crash.

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:28.400
In a 2022 interview, Laura Linney&nbsp;
was asked if her character, Wendy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:32.240
still loved Marty, and if she thought&nbsp;
her family would survive. She told Elle,

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:36.720
"Yes, she does love Marty. She does love Marty.&nbsp;
I think their relationship goes through many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.720 --> 00:06:41.040
different incarnations, and they are bound to&nbsp;
each other, and they're sort of all they have.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:44.480
They just have each other, really.&nbsp;
And I think Wendy feels that way."

00:06:44.480 --> 00:06:48.560
Linney also revealed that she relates&nbsp;
to Wendy in many ways, telling Elle,

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:52.320
"Very much like Wendy, I believe in&nbsp;
that family, as messed up as they are.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.320 --> 00:06:56.080
As an actress, I root for the family.&nbsp;
As an actress, I root for that marriage,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.080 --> 00:07:00.480
whether it survives or not, whether the family&nbsp;
stays together or not, I root for them."

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:04.560
Though Linney's words don't guarantee Marty&nbsp;
and Wendy will make it out alive, we, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:06.080
are rooting for the Byrde family.

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.480
Charlotte Byrde is apparently all-in&nbsp;
on her family's business. She's even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:12.640
reconsidering going to college. After all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:16.800
why should she go when her family already has&nbsp;
a spot for her in their company? Nonetheless,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:21.520
we're all wondering how her change of mind will&nbsp;
play into the final seven episodes of the series.

00:07:21.520 --> 00:07:25.360
Though actress Sofia Hublitz, who plays&nbsp;
Charlotte, doesn't give too much away,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.360 --> 00:07:29.440
she has said something utterly intriguing&nbsp;
regarding the Byrde family's ending.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:32.080
In a 2022 interview with Elle, she revealed,

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:36.640
"It's a different experience for me because it is&nbsp;
my first major role. When we wrapped, we wrapped&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.640 --> 00:07:41.040
our final scene together as a family — I won't&nbsp;
say what it was, obviously — the scene that we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:46.000
filmed together was a scene as a family. That&nbsp;
was my last scene. It was Wendy's last scene."

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.280
It's still largely speculative, but&nbsp;
the fact that the actors filmed their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:52.640
final scene together could mean that&nbsp;
they were all still alive in the end.

00:07:53.680 --> 00:07:57.120
It's not entirely Marty's fault that&nbsp;
his family is working for the cartel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.120 --> 00:08:00.560
but one way or another, he got them&nbsp;
into this mess. For four seasons,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:04.880
he has been trying to make what he believes are&nbsp;
the best decisions to keep his family alive.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:09.280
Needless to say, it's been a rip-roaring&nbsp;
roller coaster, and we all want to know if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:13.200
the series can stick the landing. Bateman&nbsp;
said in a 2020 IndieWire interview,

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:16.800
"I do know where everything is going to&nbsp;
end [...] I was interested in the big&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:20.160
question [showrunner Chris Mundy]&nbsp;
has the opportunity to answer:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:24.080
Are they going to get away with it, or are&nbsp;
they going to pay a bill? What does he want&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:29.200
to message to the audience about the consequences&nbsp;
of what the Byrdes have done – or lack thereof?"

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:31.280
Viewers have similar questions, as it seems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:35.760
unlikely that this family will receive a&nbsp;
happily-ever-after. Bateman also revealed,

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:39.920
"We had some great conversations about that,&nbsp;
and he's got really good ideas about that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:39.920 --> 00:08:45.280
Specifically, what kind of happens at the end&nbsp;
of the last episode: I know, and it's great."

00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.200
If Bateman believes the ending is great,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:50.640
then we'll take his word for it.&nbsp;
The countdown to the end is on.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:08:54.080
In a 2022 interview with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.240
showrunner Chris Mundy teased what's to come&nbsp;
in the final batch of episodes, explaining,

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:02.560
"I always want closure. I don't want to&nbsp;
feel messed with. I want to feel like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.560 --> 00:09:05.040
'OK, that was the end.' So hopefully people will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:08.880
feel closure by the end — whether&nbsp;
they like it or not, I don't know."

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:12.640
Mundy also opened up about the&nbsp;
show's central relationship, saying,

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:17.040
"In terms of tone, we're going deeper into&nbsp;
the family and their bonds. Is family the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:22.000
ultimate bond? Is friendship? Is marriage?&nbsp;
At what point is it almost unhealthy to stay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:26.240
even if you love somebody? We're going to delve&nbsp;
into that with Marty and Wendy. Hopefully,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:30.640
the back half will still be fun and exciting, but&nbsp;
also really emotional for the Byrdes and Ruth."

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.400
Thankfully, Netflix has already released a teaser&nbsp;
trailer for "Ozark" Season 4, Part 2, which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:41.040
mostly features a distressed Ruth on the verge of&nbsp;
blowing everything up. It also touches on events&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:46.480
that plagued the Byrdes and the Langmores in the&nbsp;
first half of Season 4. Ruth says in the trailer,

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:49.680
"My childhood traumas are not like yours."

00:09:49.680 --> 00:09:54.000
If this is any indication, Ruth will likely seek&nbsp;
vengeance for everything that's happened to her.

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:57.760
"You see, I'm a cursed Langmore."

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:00.960
It remains to be seen what's in&nbsp;
store for Marty and his family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:00.960 --> 00:10:05.440
but it would be a miracle if everyone makes&nbsp;
it out alive. The reign of the Byrdes and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.240
Langmores is coming to a conclusion with the&nbsp;
final batch of "Ozark" episodes on April 29.

